  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "There are NNN children and Chef wants to give them 111 candy each. Chef already has XXX candies with him. To buy the rest, he visits a candy shop. In the shop, packets containing **exactly** 444 candies are available.\n\nDetermine the **minimum** number of candy packets Chef must buy so that he is able to give 111 candy to each of the NNN children.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nThe first and only line of each test case contains two integers NNN and XXX — the number of children and the number of candies Chef already has.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output the **minimum** number of candy packets Chef must buy so that he is able to give 111 candy to each of the NNN children.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤10001 \\leq T \\leq 10001≤T≤1000",
      "1≤N,X≤1001 \\leq N, X \\leq 1001≤N,X≤100"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "4\n20 12\n10 100\n10 9\n20 9",
        "output": "2\n0\n1\n3",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 111: Chef must buy 222 more packets after which he will have 202020 candies which will be enough to distribute 111 candy to each of the 202020 children.\nTest Case 222: Chef does not need to buy more packets since he already has 100100100 candies which are enough to distribute 111 candy to each of the 101010 children.\nTest Case 333: Chef must buy 111 more packet after which he will have 131313 candies which will be enough to distribute 111 candy to each of the 101010 children.\nTest Case 444: Chef must buy 333 more packets after which he will have 212121 candies which will be enough to distribute 111 candy to each of the 202020 children."
      }
    ]
  },
